    "summary": "A few of the comments that stood out to us yesterday: \"I did the rear disc conversion on this truck many years ago. It was done using front hubs (bolt right on) and RRC /DI rear rotors and calipers. I never liked the way Land Rover cheaped out on the factory rear Salisbury disc setup by using the narrow drive flanges with short splines that strip out easily and short spindles with narrow spaced bearings... That's why I used to do it this way, retaining the far better wide drive flanges and longer axle spline engagement, with wet splines. The&#8230;\" 14 51rvr commented on 1993 Land Rover Defender 110 NAS 5-Speed \"When I was a kid, I remember overhearing a conversation between my mom and dad about it being time for a new car. Final words to my dad were \"I don't care what it is as long as it's a station wagon!'. Boy, just imagine if he had come home with this one!!\" 10 PanteraMike74 commented on No Reserve: 31-Mile 2025 Audi RS6 Avant GT \"I use to own that car. I bought it from the original owner who owned it in Sacramento California. When I sold it through a Ferrari shop located in San Mateo it went back east . At the time it still had it’s original paint and by looking at the pictures I think it still does.. I had both seats redone in the original material that I obtained from Italy.. i remember the car well. ( I designed the battery closing panel as I could not find back then an original battery cover.. The car never had&#8230;\" 9 dinoverde commented on 1972 Alfa Romeo Montreal",
